      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Low-Tiers could be characterized by a more rugged, weathered appearance, with skin tones ranging from a dull, earthy brown to a pale, almost translucent quality, as if they're perpetually on the verge of sunburn or malnutrition. Their hair could be coarse and wiry, with a tendency to grow in uneven, unruly clumps, and facial features might be more angular and pronounced, with high cheekbones, prominent foreheads, and a general air of rough-hewn, unpolished beauty. Their eyes might be a dull, milky yellow or a deep, piercing brown, with a tendency to be sunken or bloodshot, giving them a perpetually tired, world-weary look. To further emphasize their \"raw\" nature, you could also consider giving them a more pronounced body odor, a tendency to grow body hair in unusual places, or a general air of unkemptness and dishevelment.",
